{# How to fill in the arguments of a call. The refused calls give an argument name that the
   schema does not have, a text where the schema asks for a list, or a value in extra quotes. #}
Filling in the arguments of a call

{% if has('read_tool') %}
When you are not sure of the arguments of a tool, call {{ tool('read_tool') }} with its name. It gives each argument, its type and the arguments that the tool requires.

{% endif %}
1. Give only the argument names that the tool gives. An argument with another name is refused.
2. Give each required argument.
3. Where the tool asks for a list, give a list, also for one value. Write queries ["lease"]. Do not write queries "lease".
4. Where the tool asks for a number or true or false, give the value with no quotes. Write filename_only true. Do not write filename_only "true".
5. Do not put quotes inside a text value. Write status done. Do not write status "\"done\"".
6. Keep each value inside the limits of its tool, such as the most items of a list.

When a call is refused, the error names the argument and what is wrong with it. Correct that argument, and then send the call.

{% if has('search_agent_tools') %}
{{ tool('search_agent_tools') }} requires query, a task description of up to 160 characters.
It returns relevant tool names and descriptions. Read a tool before using unfamiliar arguments.
```json
{"query":"Find a passage late in one long document."}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_tool') %}
{{ tool('read_tool') }} requires name, the exact name of one available tool.
It returns the description and full input schema, including allowed values, defaults and required fields.
```json
{"name":"read_documents"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_skills') %}
{{ tool('search_skills') }} accepts query, up to 160 characters. Omission or empty text lists every available skill.
It returns method names and descriptions.
```json
{}
```
```json
{"query":"Read a long document and continue its matching passage."}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_skill') %}
{{ tool('read_skill') }} requires name, the exact name returned by skill discovery.
It returns the method instructions, tool arguments and examples.
```json
{"name":"passages"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('write_note') %}
{{ tool('write_note') }} requires text, with 1 to 2,000 characters. It saves evidence and unresolved questions for later context.
Include source identities and the next useful call when that context must survive compaction.
```json
{"text":"The approval passage is in the returned document range. Verify its original writer before attributing it."}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('ask_user') %}
{{ tool('ask_user') }} requires question, with 1 to 500 characters.
options optionally supplies up to six answers, each with 1 to 80 characters. Ask for a missing task choice that the sources cannot resolve.
It pauses the conversation until the person replies.
```json
{"question":"Which collection should supply the requested report?","options":["alpha","beta"]}
```
{% endif %}
